rev21 (VR R20 item 1c, 2026-09-09). the user, wearing 1.0.1.24: the hammer's
swing came down about the wrong axis and sank the whole weapon, so "the butt of
the handle hangs on the ground". The shell's fix pivots at the hand and drops
the grip by nothing -- which means the head now finishes ABOVE the floor on a
waist-height chop, and vanilla's ground line test stops at the tip. One pure
addition to func_80842DF4 extends that probe past the tip by gSohVRHammerProbe
game units, VR + motion hands + hammer only, with vanilla's own surface filters
and vanilla's own response.

rev20 (VR R19, 2026-09-08). the user, wearing 1.0.1.23: "The Megaton hammer
works with either trigger and I see the wind/swish animation, but the hammer
doesn't do the hitting-the-ground swing animation. It stays in my arm,
upright." R18 restored vanilla's authored hammer swing; the authored swing
moves the ARM, and the arm in VR is the controller. So the hammer gets what
R9-R12 built for the sword -- a shell-side envelope that moves the HELD MESH --
started from a counter bumped at func_80837948, vanilla's one melee-animation
site, and its ground hit counted at func_80842A28. Nothing about vanilla's
hammer is reimplemented: the animation, the swish, the quake, the shockwave and
the melee quads all stay whole, and the quads and the ground line test follow
the envelope for free because vanilla builds them through the L_HAND limb
matrix, which is the controller.

rev17 (VR R16, 2026-09-07). Four of the user's reports from wearing 1.0.1.20,
three of which land in this patch:
  * THE CROSSHAIR WAS INVISIBLE, and so was vanilla's hookshot reticle, for
    one reason: Player_DrawHookshotReticle emits to OVERLAY_DISP and overlay
    0043 detaches the overlay buffer from the world list in VR gameplay to
    render it as the flat HUD plane. A world-space draw left in it is
    composited onto a billboard in front of the wearer's face. The VR sites
    get Player_VrDrawAimReticle -- vanilla's routine, POLY_XLU_DISP -- and
    the Matrix_Translate(500, 300, 0) rev16 left out (the routine's start
    point is D_801260C8 = (-500, -100, 0), which vanilla cancels at every one
    of its own call sites). Three sites now: bow/slingshot, hookshot/longshot
    (ungated in VR -- a wearer never enters func_8002DD78's aim mode) and the
    boomerang.
  * THE BOOMERANG THREW ON THE RELEASE, through vanilla's hold-to-aim, which
    in a headset is a Z-target-like chirp, a letterbox and a delay. The pull
    synthesises the release when the aim ray answers; func_80834F2C never
    enters func_80834EB8; and Player_SetParallel -- NA_SE_SY_ATTENTION_ON, the
    chirp itself -- is skipped for a VR-aimed throw.
  * THE GAUNTLET PLATES AND BOOTS FLOATED. Player_DrawImpl emits them after
    SkelAnime_DrawFlexLod, from the matrices the skeleton left behind, so
    nulling *dList in the limb override never reached them.
  * THE WORLD NOW TURNS WITH LINK when the GAME turns him (ladder, ledge,
    hang). The facing pin stands down in those states by design; nothing
    followed the 0x8000 snap a descent writes, so the wearer climbed down
    facing away from the ladder. One writer publishes a delta and a sequence
    number and the shell eases its own world yaw by it.

rev2 (VR R3, 2026-09-03). the user's 1.0.1.3 verdict was that R2b had moved the
viewpoint to Link's face and stopped: "if i turn around, i can see a warped
inside of my body... the only part of my body i should be seeing is probably my
hands... what you've patch-worked here is basically 3rd person mode except the
