rev10 (VR R10, 2026-09-05). One ruling, and it is the shape of the whole round:

  * "THE JUMP ATTACK WHEN Z-TARGETING, THE CAMERA SHOULD REFLECT A JUMP ATTACK
    -- SOME VERTICAL MOVEMENT OF THE CAMERA. IT SHOULD MATCH VANILLA." rev8's
    early-out in Player_ActionHandler_10 removed the authored jump slash, and
    with it the LEAP: func_8083BA90 is what sets PLAYER_STATE3_MIDAIR and the
    xz/y velocities of 5. The VR eye rides the actor root, so a Link who never
    left the ground gives a wearer who never left the ground.

    The action runs again. What rev8 was right about is preserved by three
    mechanisms that were already there or are added here: the authored ARM
    animation is invisible because the hand limb is pinned; the authored QUADS
    never register because z_player_lib.c refuses vanilla's fattened AT quads
    while motion combat covers the weapon (so the blade remains the only thing
    that damages -- the R5 "two attacks per press" defect cannot return through
    this door); and the VOICE is arbitrated, because func_8083BA90 ends with
    Player_PlayVoiceSfx(NA_SE_VO_LI_SWORD_L) and the chop seam would otherwise
    play a second one. The arbiter is a DEFERRED yell rather than a mute: the
    action handlers run inside this->actionFunc, i.e. after the seam, so on the
    press tick the seam cannot know whether vanilla's will fire -- it has its own
    conditions. The seam stays silent, records the counter, and yells one tick
    later only if the counter did not move.

