+ * the user: "as soon as you select the boomerang, it throws once, every
+ * time." The cause is vanilla, and it is not the direct throw itself.
+ * Player_UpperAction_ChangeHeldItem sets sUseHeldItem through
+ * VB_USE_HELD_ITEM_AFTER_CHANGE the moment the item-change animation has
+ * swapped the model -- on an N64 that is the whole point (you are still
+ * holding the C button you pressed, so the bow draws and the boomerang
+ * enters its aim), and it arrives here as a use that NOBODY asked for,
+ * because in VR the press came from the item compass or from one tick of a
+ * C button and the trigger is not down at all. rev17's synthesised release
+ * then turns that free use into a free throw.
