+ * the user, on 1.0.1.14: "Link no longer makes the YELL on the button
+ * attack." rev8 routed the sound through vanilla's own func_80833A20,
+ * which is the right instinct (its selection of the light and heavy swing
+ * SFX is vanilla's, and duplicating it would drift) and carries two guards
+ * that have nothing to do with a VR press:
+ *
+ *   1. it plays nothing unless meleeWeaponState is currently 0, and
+ *   2. it plays no VOICE while meleeWeaponAnimation is in 16..19
+ *      (FLIPSLASH_START .. JUMPSLASH_FINISH).
+ *
+ * rev10 let vanilla's Z-target jump slash run again, and that writes
+ * meleeWeaponAnimation = PLAYER_MWA_JUMPSLASH_START. Nothing writes it
+ * back, because every other writer lives inside the authored attack machine
+ * rev5 retires for a covered weapon. So from the first jump attack of a
+ * session, guard 2 was permanently true and every B press was a swish with
+ * no voice -- for the rest of the session.
+ *
+ * This reproduces func_80833A20's SELECTION (the part that is vanilla's
+ * judgement) and drops its GATING (the part that is about vanilla's own
+ * animation state machine, which is exactly what VR does not have). The
+ * caller sets meleeWeaponState itself, separately, so state and sound stop
+ * being able to veto each other. sohHard picks the heavy pair, which is
+ * unk_845 >= 3 in vanilla: NA_SE_IT_SWORD_SWING_HARD and
+ * NA_SE_VO_LI_SWORD_L, the loud yell the user asked to keep. */
+static void Player_VrAttackVoice(Player* sohThis, s32 sohHard) {
+    u16 sohItemSfx;
+    u16 sohVoiceSfx;
