+ * That is a precise description of two correct mechanisms running at once.
+ * R5's physical blade (overlay 0048) damages from where the hand actually
+ * is, and R4's swing-presses-B path still ran the AUTHORED attack: the
+ * animation swept Link's arm along its scripted arc while the hand limb
+ * stayed pinned to the controller, so what a headset sees is the trail
+ * flying off along an arc the visible sword never travels. Two attacks per
+ * swing, and the one you can see is the one that is not yours.
+ *
+ * The donor made this choice first and made it at the root: with a covered
+ * weapon its func_8083BB20 returns 0, which retires the entire authored
+ * attack state machine -- combo chains, root motion, the stab lunge -- in
+ * one line, precisely BECAUSE the damage comes from the blade instead.
+ * R4 shipped the opposite on purpose (its notes say so plainly: nothing is
+ * re-implemented, so nothing can be re-implemented wrongly) and that was
+ * the right call for a round with no physical blade. R5 built the blade and
+ * did not withdraw the other half. This is that withdrawal.
+ *
+ * COVERED is deliberately narrow, exactly as the donor's is: the three
+ * swords (Master 1, Kokiri 2, Biggoron/Giant's Knife 3). The Deku stick and
+ * the hammer keep their vanilla attacks whole, because nothing physical has
+ * been built for them and an unattackable hammer is worse than an authored
+ * one. It also requires a TRACKED hand and gSohVRBladeDamage: if the Sense
+ * pair drops out mid-fight the authored attack returns on the very next
+ * tick rather than leaving the player with no attack at all.
+ *
+ * And it requires the weapon to be IN HAND. With the sword sheathed
+ * Player_GetMeleeWeaponHeld is 0, so this is false, so the R4 path below
+ * still fires the authored draw-and-slash -- which is how the sword gets
+ * out of its scabbard in the first place. Suppressing that too would leave
+ * a swing with nothing to swing. */
+static s32 Player_VrMotionCombatCovered(Player* sohThis) {
+    s32 sohHeld;
+
+    if ((gSohVRFpActive == 0) || (gSohVRMotionHands == 0) || (gSohVRBladeDamage == 0)) {
+        return 0;
+    }
+    if (gSohVRHandValid[(gSohVRLeftHanded != 0) ? 0 : 1] == 0) {
+        return 0;
+    }
+    if (sohThis->actor.category != ACTORCAT_PLAYER) {
+        return 0;
+    }
+    sohHeld = Player_GetMeleeWeaponHeld(sohThis);
+    return (sohHeld == 1) || (sohHeld == 2) || (sohHeld == 3);
